# Climate — the rule that matters

**Moisture is advected, never painted on by latitude.** Air picks up
water over the sea, travels downwind, rains some out at every step, and
arrives inland already depleted. Latitude only sets how readily air rains
out, not how much water is there.

That is the only way to get the thing that separates Earth's climate map
from a set of stripes: the subtropical dry belt is not a girdle. A
continent's windward coast is wet and its leeward coast dry.

Do not add a distance-to-ocean falloff, drop `recycling`, or drop the
two-season solve.

The full invariant list, the model, and the bake-time tier:
[docs/climate.md](../../docs/stages/climate.md). Do not restate it here.

Judge from `bun run preview climate` — the moisture field on its own. The
finished biome map compresses the middle of the range, so a real
improvement can look like no change.
